        "code": {
          "text": "Left heel pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pain for about 3–4 weeks at the anteromedial calcaneus, described as feeling like standing on a stone. Worse with the first steps in the morning, after long sitting in a patrol car, long shifts, foot patrol, and heavy boots. Eases after 10–15 minutes of walking, then becomes a dull ache by the end of the shift."
      }
